---
title: Smoked baby back ribs
servings: 4
tags: [american, pork, smoker, fourth of july, summer]
cuisine: american
source: Baby Back Ribs (Oven or Smoker) by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/baby-back-ribs-smoker-or-oven.html
---

== Rub ==

Mix the @sugar{3%tbsp}, @salt{2%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1.5%tbsp}, @garlic powder{1.5%tsp}, @onion powder{1.5%tsp}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @ground mustard{1/2%tsp} and @cayenne pepper{1/2%tsp} in a bowl.

== Ribs ==

Heat the #smoker{} to 225°F (110°C).

Pull the membrane off the underside of the @baby back ribs{2%racks}.

Coat both sides with about half the rub. Let them sit ~{15%minutes}, then coat with the rest.

Smoke the ribs ~{2%hours}.

Double-wrap each rack in heavy-duty foil and smoke ~{1.5%hours} more. Hot fat can run out of the foil, so handle them carefully.

Open the foil, leaving the ribs on it. Brush the top of each rack with about 3 tbsp of the @barbecue sauce{6%tbsp}(plus more for serving). Turn the foil edges up into a tray.

Smoke ~{45-60%minutes} more, until tender.

> They are done when a rack lifted from the middle with tongs bends easily and the meat cracks on top.

Rest ~{10%minutes}, then cut between the bones and serve with more sauce.
